cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the essay it
  implements.
title: "lat — Language as a Tool"
abstract: >-
  A local, read-only Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that serves a curated
  catalogue of natural-language and poetic "thinking patterns", classified by a
  closed set of cognitive axes, for reframing a problem through a contrasting
  language or form. The selection method is an inverted soft Sapir-Whorf model:
  the grammatical bias of the input language is treated not as a constraint on
  the speaker but as a choosable instrument, and a structurally orthogonal
  pattern is selected because it forces the distinction the input language leaves
  implicit.
type: software
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: "2026-08-22"
